{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"California security deposit cap for residential tenancies","requirement":"A landlord may not demand or receive security, however denominated, above one month's rent, in addition to the first month's rent paid on or before initial occupancy.","key_value":"1 month's rent, plus first month's rent","coverage_conditions":"Security for a rental agreement for residential property used as the tenant's dwelling; applies to all landlords.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Advance payment of not less than six months' rent where the lease term is six months or longer; mutual agreement for alterations; the two-month cap for qualifying small landlords; security collected or demanded before July 1, 2024.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2024-07-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5","quoted_span":"(c) (1) Except as provided in paragraph (2), (3), or (5), a landlord shall not demand or receive security, however denominated, in an amount or value in excess of an amount equal to one month’s rent, in addition to any rent for the first month paid on or before initial occupancy.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Two-month security cap for qualifying small landlords","requirement":"A landlord who is a natural person, or an LLC whose members are all natural persons, and who owns no more than two residential rental properties with at most four dwelling units total may not demand or receive security above two months' rent plus the first month's rent.","key_value":"2 months' rent, plus first month's rent","coverage_conditions":"Landlord is a natural person or an LLC whose members are all natural persons, and owns no more than two residential rental properties collectively containing no more than four dwelling units offered for rent.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":4,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Landlord owns no more than two residential rental properties; natural person or LLC of natural persons"},"exemptions":"Subparagraph (A) does not apply if the prospective tenant is a service member; a landlord may not refuse to rent to a service member because of that limit.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2024-07-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5","quoted_span":"(5) (A) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), a landlord shall not demand or receive security, however denominated, in an amount or value in excess of an amount equal to two months’ rent, in addition to any rent for the first month paid on or before initial occupancy if the landlord meets both of the following requirements:","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Higher security charged to service members: disclosure and refund","requirement":"A landlord charging a service member higher than standard security because of credit history, credit score, housing history or similar factors must give a written statement of the higher amount and the reason by the date the lease is signed, and return the extra amount after no more than six months of residency if rent is current.","key_value":"extra security returned after no more than 6 months' residency","coverage_conditions":"Service members (Military and Veterans Code § 400) renting residential property in which the service member will reside.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Service member tenants"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-04-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5","quoted_span":"(4) On or after April 1, 2025, if a landlord or its agent charges a service member who rents residential property in which the service member will reside a higher than standard or advertised security pursuant to paragraph (1) due to the credit history, credit score, housing history, or other factor related to the tenant, the landlord shall provide the tenant with a written statement, on or before the date the lease is signed, of the amount of the higher security and an explanation why the higher security amount is being charged.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Pre-move-out initial inspection of rental unit","requirement":"Within a reasonable time after either party notifies intent to terminate, or before the lease term ends, the landlord must tell the tenant in writing of the right to request an initial inspection and to be present, and on request must inspect no earlier than two weeks before termination with at least 48 hours' written notice.","key_value":"no earlier than 2 weeks before termination; 48 hours' notice","coverage_conditions":"Tenants of residential rental property; triggered by notice of intent to terminate or before the end of the lease term.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Requirements do not apply when the tenancy is terminated under CCP § 1161(2), (3) or (4); landlord's duties are discharged if the tenant does not request an inspection.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5","quoted_span":"(f) (1) Within a reasonable time after notification of either party’s intention to terminate the tenancy, or before the end of the lease term, the landlord shall notify the tenant in writing of the tenant’s option to request an initial inspection and of the tenant’s right to be present at the inspection. At a reasonable time, but no earlier than two weeks before the termination or the end of lease date, the landlord, or an agent of the landlord, shall, upon the request of the tenant, make an initial inspection of the premises prior to any final inspection the landlord makes after the tenant has vacated the premises.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"21-day deadline to return deposit with itemized statement","requirement":"No later than 21 calendar days after the tenant vacates, the landlord must furnish an itemized statement of the basis for and amount of the security and its disposition, return any remaining portion, and supply supporting documents and photographs for deductions.","key_value":"21 calendar days","coverage_conditions":"All residential landlords holding security; deadline runs from the day the tenant vacates.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Repair/cleaning documentation need not be provided if those deductions total $125 or less, or if the tenant waived that right after a termination notice; documentation requirements do not apply to tenancies ended under CCP § 1161(2), (3) or (4).","penalty":"The landlord shall not be entitled to claim any amount of the security if the landlord, in bad faith, fails to comply with this subdivision.","effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5","quoted_span":"(h) (1) No later than 21 calendar days after the tenant has vacated the premises, but not earlier than the time that either the landlord or the tenant provides a notice to terminate the tenancy under Section 1946 or 1946.1, Section 1161 of the Code of Civil Procedure, or not earlier than 60 calendar days prior to the expiration of a fixed-term lease, the landlord shall furnish the tenant, a copy of an itemized statement indicating the basis for, and the amount of, any security received and the disposition of the security, and shall return any remaining portion of the security to the tenant as follows:","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
